gate how can people take that the  NFL is taking abuse against women  seriously I know the NFL they're not  trying to push people who do bad things  though abuse against women they're not  trying to push those guys on the field  have you spoken to Kareem hunt no I have  it do you want to I would love to help  anyone that's willing to go to long haul  well we reached out to the NFL which  confirmed that rice shared his story is  part of the league's domestic violence  education program the NFL says it rice  has an important message to share and  that his commitment is sincere and if  you're a victim of domestic violence and  you need help you can call the national  domestic violence hotline that's one  eight hundred seven nine nine seventy  two thirty three I also thought that his  commitment is very sincere he does a lot  of speaking to NFL players and to  college players he's coaching high  school football at his old high school  he volunteers there but I was really  impressed with janay rice I have to say  she's not a little mouse burger robot  wife because I couldn't understand after  knowing and seeing that video how she  was able to take him back and and she  says that this was the first and only  time I really pressed them on that  because I said that defies everything  that we know about domestic violence in  any type of relationship and they both  insist that was the case well remember  he not only punched her exactly knocked  her unconscious in the first videotape  that we saw was just of Ray Rice  dragging her and I had that interview  with Roger Goodell I remember that at  the time but I am glad just they seem  like they are in a good place and Tre  are getting therapy they need to discuss  this and maybe try and help people learn  something more about domestic violence  whether they were a victim of it  themselves and then repeated that  behavior and how to end it and that's  what they mean about hard work to your  point I mean they've had extensive  cou